<p class="paper_abstract">This track invites conceptual, empirical, methodological and interdisciplinary contributions that critically examine the role of entrepreneurship in advancing sustainable development during the remaining years of the SDGs and in shaping post-2030 sustainability agendas. The track aims to connects entrepreneurial agency with the wider institutional, societal and ecological systems in which entrepreneurship takes place.</p>
<p class="paper_abstract">A central question for the track is not simply whether entrepreneurship can contribute to sustainable development, but how, for whom, under what conditions and with what consequences. We invite academic researchers, corporate professionals, startup founders, government officials to take this as an opportunity to talk about their work, to explore the challenges and provide reflections on practical solutions. Contributions are particularly welcome that generate lessons from the SDG era and offer insights into the role sustainable entrepreneurship may play in shaping more inclusive, resilient and sustainable futures beyond 2030.</p>
